and you lied to me.

263
00:12:49,478 --> 00:12:50,478
Oh, mom.

264
00:12:50,646 --> 00:12:52,731
You broke into my home
and tried to steal it.

265
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:53,940
Oh, George.

266
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:55,335
You told her we went over there?

267
00:12:55,359 --> 00:12:57,027
Oh, George Jr.

268
00:12:57,236 --> 00:12:58,946
I didn't say nothing.
I was cool.

269
00:12:59,154 --> 00:13:00,781
I am loving this.

270
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,741
I don't want this woman
in my house anymore.

271
00:13:02,991 --> 00:13:04,785
- She is my mother.
- She is the devil.

272
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:06,745
And what if the kids
want to see her?

273
00:13:07,871 --> 00:13:08,622
Fine.

274
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:10,791
Schedule it
for when I'm not here.

275
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:12,542
Or when I'm dead.

276
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,094
And quit drinking my coffee.

277
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:33,438
Turn off your train,
we've got to talk.

278
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,149
About what?

279
00:13:36,358 --> 00:13:37,859
Mom is so upset
about dad and meemaw,

280
00:13:38,068 --> 00:13:39,361
she might want a divorce.

281
00:13:39,611 --> 00:13:40,988
No one's getting divorced.

282
00:13:41,196 --> 00:13:42,196
How do you know?

283
00:13:43,824 --> 00:13:45,409
Great, now I have
to throw that out.

284
00:13:46,576 --> 00:13:49,663
Mother-in-laws are always held
in low regard by the father.

285
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:51,957
It rarely leads
to a breakup of the family.

286
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:53,332
Missy: He's right.

287
00:13:53,375 --> 00:13:55,711
Fred and Wilma
are still happily married.

288
00:13:56,795 --> 00:13:57,504
I think if we can figure out

289
00:13:57,713 --> 00:13:59,631
a way for dad to get
meemaw's brisket recipe,

290
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,091
this all goes away.

291
00:14:01,383 --> 00:14:03,510
I don't see how
we can accomplish that.

292
00:14:05,429 --> 00:14:06,179
Put that down.

293
00:14:06,388 --> 00:14:07,431
That's not a toy.

294
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:08,390
Sure it is.

295
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:09,975
Choo choo.

296
00:14:10,642 --> 00:14:12,311
Meemaw: Choo choo...

297
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:14,688
Choo choo.

298
00:14:15,439 --> 00:14:17,357
Open wide, moonpie.

299
00:14:17,566 --> 00:14:20,027
Here comes the choo choo train.

300
00:14:20,235 --> 00:14:22,154
Choo choo.

301
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,197
Mmm. Isn't that good?

302
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:28,702
That's meemaw's famous brisket.

303
00:14:29,286 --> 00:14:30,787
Would you like
the secret recipe?

304
00:14:32,331 --> 00:14:34,875
You promise not to tell anybody?

305
00:14:35,292 --> 00:14:37,669
Of course you're not gonna
tell anybody.

306
00:14:37,878 --> 00:14:41,214
I start with a tablespoon
of cumin,

307
00:14:41,673 --> 00:14:44,760
and then a cup
of brown sugar, and...

308
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:46,219
I know the recipe.

309
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:47,346
What?

310
00:14:47,554 --> 00:14:48,555
She told it to me.

311
00:14:48,764 --> 00:14:49,473
When?

312
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:51,683
February 14, 1982.

313
00:14:52,267 --> 00:14:54,353
I was 23 months old,
it was Valentine's day,

314
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:55,961
and mom and dad
went out for dinner.

315
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,273
You were there.
Don't you remember?

316
00:15:03,445 --> 00:15:04,654
I got nothing.

317
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:07,115
You can really remember
when you were that little?

318
00:15:07,324 --> 00:15:08,575
Uh-huh. You were there, too.

319
00:15:08,784 --> 00:15:10,584
You were still struggling
with potty training.

320
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:12,245
I don't think so.

321
00:15:12,454 --> 00:15:15,582
Oh, yes. Meemaw used to call you
Mr. Soggy pants.

322
00:15:15,791 --> 00:15:16,541
Nuh-uh.

323
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:18,251
Uaughsy Mr. Soggy pants.

324
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,961
Quit it. This is serious.

325
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:22,005
Sheldon, you've got
to tell dad that recipe.

326
00:15:22,506 --> 00:15:24,758
But meemaw told me
it was a secret.

327
00:15:24,966 --> 00:15:27,719
If you don't, and mom and dad
get a divorce, it's your fault.

328
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:30,055
All right.

329
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:31,263
Fine.

330
00:15:32,808 --> 00:15:34,810
Good job, soggy pants.

331
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:39,981
Dad, could you please
come into the living room?

332
00:15:40,524 --> 00:15:41,524
What for?

333
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,846
My brain
did something impressive

334
00:15:42,901 --> 00:15:44,569
and I'd like to share it
with you.

335
00:15:46,029 --> 00:15:47,322
Hmm.

336
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:54,579
What are you doing here?

337
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,123
Same as you.

338
00:15:56,331 --> 00:15:58,125
I want to see
what his brain did.

339
00:15:58,333 --> 00:15:59,418
Please have a seat.

340
00:16:01,378 --> 00:16:02,587
All right.

341
00:16:06,216 --> 00:16:07,216
George sr.: Well?

342
00:16:07,509 --> 00:16:09,553
I know meemaw's brisket recipe.

343
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:10,470
What?

344
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:11,471
No, you don't.

345
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,140
Yes, I do.

346
00:16:13,348 --> 00:16:15,142
And in order to bring peace
to this family,

347
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:16,935
I'm prepared to make it public.

348
00:16:17,144 --> 00:16:17,936
You're bluffing.

349
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:19,563
One tablespoon of cumin,

350
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:20,772
one cup of brown sugar,

351
00:16:20,981 --> 00:16:22,774
two tablespoons
of smoked paprika...

352
00:16:22,983 --> 00:16:23,983
Okay, okay, stop.

353
00:16:24,109 --> 00:16:25,109
No, no, no. Keep going.

354
00:16:25,152 --> 00:16:26,778
How do you know
the recipe, Shelly?

355
00:16:26,987 --> 00:16:29,823
Meemaw told it to me
on Valentine's day, 1982.

356
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:31,825
You were out with dad
seeing cannonball run

357
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,160
at the dollar theater.

358
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:35,662
That's impossible, you weren't
even two years old.

359
00:16:35,871 --> 00:16:37,414
Three tablespoons
of dried mustard,

360
00:16:37,622 --> 00:16:39,082
one cup of lone star beer...

361
00:16:39,291 --> 00:16:40,291
Okay.

362
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:42,918
Okay.

363
00:16:43,879 --> 00:16:45,046
Go ahead.

364
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,174
Give it to your father.

365
00:16:47,466 --> 00:16:49,009
I can write it down for you.

366
00:16:50,969 --> 00:16:52,345
That's okay, I don't want it.

367
00:16:52,554 --> 00:16:54,764
You have got to be kidding me.

368
00:16:54,973 --> 00:16:56,200
Connie, you've had
every opportunity

369
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:57,702
to give me that recipe
and you never did,

370
00:16:57,726 --> 00:16:59,495
because you've always
treated me like an outsider.

371
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:00,312
No, she has not.

372
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,605
Oh, of course I have.

373
00:17:01,813 --> 00:17:02,981
See? She admits it.

374
00:17:03,398 --> 00:17:05,025
Damn right, I do.

375
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,986
Never thought you were good
enough for my daughter.

376
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,156
There you were, riding around
on that dumb motorcycle,

377
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,115
knocking her up.

378
00:17:12,324 --> 00:17:13,783
Why don't you kids
go in the kitchen

379
00:17:13,992 --> 00:17:15,312
and fix yourselves
some ice cream?

380
00:17:15,494 --> 00:17:16,995
I'm not going anywhere.

381
00:17:19,331 --> 00:17:21,208
Hey. I get it.

382
00:17:22,334 --> 00:17:23,502
I have a daughter.

383
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,338
I wouldn't want her bringing
home someone like that.

384
00:17:28,006 --> 00:17:30,258
But I've come
a hell of a long way since then.

385
00:17:34,304 --> 00:17:35,764
Okay, you're right.

386
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,560
George.

387
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,106
I'm sorry.

388
00:17:48,235 --> 00:17:50,904
That means more to me
than any recipe.

389
00:17:52,614 --> 00:17:53,657
Come here.

390
00:18:01,164 --> 00:18:02,767
Adult Sheldon:
Don't let the hug fool you.

391
00:18:02,791 --> 00:18:06,127
The minute she went home,
he made me give him the recipe.

392
00:18:09,923 --> 00:18:13,009
Here we go, maiden voyage.

393
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:17,055
Mmm, mmm.

394
00:18:17,264 --> 00:18:18,515
Hot damn.

395
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:21,184
George sr.: Hot damn.

396
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:26,439
Hot damn!

397
00:18:26,648 --> 00:18:28,984
Mary: George! Language.

398
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,317
Sheldon.

399
00:18:30,986 --> 00:18:31,986
Want some?

400
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:34,573
Uh, no, thank you.
I'm not hungry.

